  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 241 PM MST TUE NOV 17 2026\nUnsettled conditions continue as the upper-level low moves east\nof the area Friday, bringing northwesterly flow aloft and light\nshowers. With snow levels expected to be around 3000-3500 ft \nMSL before the precipitation moves out, valley wintry mix and \nmountain snow is currently forecast. Precipitation will \ngradually taper off through the day Friday. The pattern will \ncontinue to evolve quickly thereafter, with a shortwave upper- \nlevel ridge Saturday providing dry conditions until the next \nstrong low pressure system begins to moves on shore late \nSaturday. Southwesterly flow aloft will move over the region \nwith increasing precipitation chances Saturday night and lasting\nthrough Monday. Another brief upper-level ridge is well agreed \nupon long range models late Monday into early Tuesday before \nanother system moves in and brings widespread precipitation \nchances yet again. Temperatures will hover near or slightly \nbelow normal in SW Idaho and 5-10 degrees below normal in SE \nOregon through the period. Breezy winds will accompany systems \npassing through.",
